From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: register 1905 wireless backhaul interface
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

multiap: register wireless backhaul STA as ieee1905 AL interface

On an agent the wireless backhaul STA netdev (e.g. bstaX) associates and
joins the AL bridge only after ieee1905d has enumerated its interfaces, and
its name matches none of the al-iface include patterns. It is therefore
never registered as a 1905 interface, so AP-Autoconfiguration Search and
Topology Discovery are only emitted on the fronthaul APs and never traverse
the backhaul to the controller: the agent never onboards (num_nodes stays 0).

map-agent already runs "/lib/wifi/multiap set_uplink wifi <ifname> <hwaddr>"
when the wireless backhaul comes up (backhaul.c). Hook that point to register
the STA netdev directly via the ieee1905 add_interface ubus method, which
binds a raw socket to the netdev (TX + RX on the backhaul) independent of
bridge multicast local-delivery behaviour.
--- a/src/script/multiap
+++ b/src/script/multiap
@@ -1533,6 +1533,16 @@
 		handle_uplink_switch $ifname
 	fi
 
+	if [ "$type" = "wifi" ] && [ -n "$ifname" ]; then
+		# Register the wireless backhaul STA (e.g. bstaX) as an ieee1905
+		# AL interface. It joins the AL bridge only after ieee1905d has
+		# enumerated interfaces and matches no al-iface include pattern,
+		# so it is otherwise never registered. Without it AP-Autoconfig
+		# Search / Topology Discovery never egress the backhaul and the
+		# agent cannot onboard to the controller.
+		ubus -t 5 call ieee1905 add_interface "{\"ifname\":\"$ifname\",\"wifi_backhaul\":true}" >/dev/null 2>&1
+	fi
+
 	update_acs
 	update_isolate_ebtables
 }
